  <page_number>85</page_number>
  <running_head>LYRICA.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <signature>F 3</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">Immane monstrum Cacus, Iberia</l>
    <l n="2" para="true">Quando reuertentem fefellit</l>
    <l n="3" para="true">Amphitryoniadem dolosis</l>
    <l n="4" para="true">Armenta carpens artibus, &amp; nigris</l>
    <l n="5" para="true">Aniri latebris sulphurei tegens:</l>
    <l n="6" para="true">Fur unde feruentes vomebat</l>
    <l n="7" para="true">Terrifico vigil ore flammas.</l>
    <l n="8" para="true">Non ille furtum, non tulit hoc scelus</l>
    <l n="9" para="true">Impune tantum: senfit enim Herculis</l>
    <l n="10" para="true">Quid nota virtus, quidve posset</l>
    <l n="11" para="true">Clava feris metuenda monstris.</l>
    <l n="12" para="true">Pares Sabaudi quum violentia</l>
    <l n="13" para="true">Specus teneret perfida militis</l>
    <l n="14" para="true">Heu! quanta late tunc per agros</l>
    <l n="15" para="true">Damna ruens dedit ille nostros:</l>
    <l n="16" para="true">Quum prepotenti firmior agmine</l>
    <l n="17" para="true">Erupit animis talibus Allobrox</l>
    <l n="18" para="true">Princeps, &amp; Hispanae phalanges,</l>
    <l n="19" para="true">Purpureaque Italum caterua.</l>
    <l n="20" para="true">Non plura ruptis obicibus mala</l>
    <l n="21" para="true">Fluctus tumentes Oceani ferunt:</l>
    <l n="22" para="true">Rhenive stagnantis refusa</l>
    <l n="23" para="true">Quum Batauas rapit unda messes.</l>
    <l n="24" para="true">Non suentes tristius irruunt</l>
    <l n="25" para="true">Venti per aequor, quum ciet Aeolus</l>
    <l n="26" para="true">Grandes procellas, atque nautis</l>
    <l n="27" para="true">Corda metu quatit inquieto.</l>
    <l n="28" para="true">Praedas abegit, diripuit domos,</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The verse is set in italic type throughout with long s printed as f in places; the transcription normalises long s to s. Some words are partly damaged by the scan (e.g. "Rhenive", "suentes", "Quum" in the margin of line 16); doubtful readings are unmarked but may be affected by the scan's blur. The line-initial capital letters are swash forms.</notes>
